<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Artaxias IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 422–428</span> · Also known as Artashir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Artaxias IV was the last Arsacid king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, ruling the Sasanian-controlled part of the country. In 428 the Armenian nobles asked the Persian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahram-v">Bahram V</a> to depose him, and the Armenian monarchy was abolished. Eastern Armenia then became the Sasanian province of Persarmenia under a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marzban">marzban</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/artaxias-iv.jpg" alt="Artaxias IV" width="320" height="285" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ջ. Ֆուզարո · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Smbat_bagratunin_tagadrum_e_artashesin.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
